    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="faq-q">Why is my margin lower than I expected?</h3>
      <p class="faq-a">Three usual suspects: (1) platform fees on small-dollar sales eat a surprisingly large percentage — a $0.55 Etsy fee on a $5 sticker is 11% gone instantly, (2) shipping the run to yourself divided across a small quantity adds real cost per print, (3) you're printing in small runs where per-unit production is highest.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="faq-q">How can I improve my margin?</h3>
      <p class="faq-a">Three levers: print in larger runs (per-unit cost drops fast), raise your price (the calculator shows exactly how much each dollar adds), or move sales off Etsy onto your own site to skip the 6.5% transaction fee.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 class="faq-q">Where does the production pricing come from?</h3>
      <p class="faq-a">Direct from Printkeg's product catalog — 396 real variants across 9 product categories. Prices are updated periodically. If you see a discrepancy with <a href="https://www.printkeg.com">printkeg.com</a>, the product page is the source of truth.</p>
